TITLE:: PltConditioning
summary:: The decisions between a descriptor and a control, one panel each
categories:: Libraries>PlotLib
related:: Overviews/PlotLib, Classes/PltTrack, Classes/PltMap, Classes/PltCut

DESCRIPTION::
A descriptor stream does not become a control by itself. Five decisions stand between
them, each looking technical and each compositional:

numberedlist::
## smoothing, here a one-pole lag with link::Classes/Lag::'s definition of lag time;
## scaling, linear or log2;
## normalising against the material, between two percentiles of this file, with the
share clipped;
## thresholding with hysteresis, with the count a bare threshold would give for
comparison;
## mapping the result through a link::Classes/ControlSpec::, or firing the events
the gate opens instead.
::

The parameters are plain setters; call code::refresh:: after changing them.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: fromSoundFile
argument:: path
argument:: descriptor
Any of link::Classes/PltObservers#*describe::.
argument:: fftSize
argument:: hop
argument:: title
argument:: width
argument:: height

METHOD:: new
argument:: values
argument:: rate
Frames per second.
argument:: name
argument:: unit
argument:: title
argument:: width
argument:: height

METHOD:: lag
60 dB of convergence in code::seconds::, as link::Classes/Lag::.
METHOD:: hysteresis
On at or above code::on::, off below code::off::.
METHOD:: rises
Where a gate opens.

INSTANCEMETHODS::
METHOD:: stages
Every stage as an Event, computed from the current parameters.
METHOD:: lag
METHOD:: warp
code::\log:: or code::\lin::.
METHOD:: lo
METHOD:: hi
Percentiles for normalising.
METHOD:: on
METHOD:: off
METHOD:: spec
METHOD:: specName
METHOD:: raw
METHOD:: rate
METHOD:: name
METHOD:: unit
METHOD:: duration
METHOD:: panelGap

EXAMPLES::
code::
c = PltConditioning.fromSoundFile(Platform.resourceDir +/+ "sounds/a11wlk01.wav").front;

// no smoothing and no gap: the bare threshold chatters
c.lag_(0).on_(0.52).off_(0.48).refresh;

// a wider gap commits less often
c.lag_(0.1).on_(0.7).off_(0.3).refresh;

c.spec_(\freq.asSpec).specName_("freq").refresh;
c.stages[\events].size;
::
